---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description="How leonlins.com and Avoid Boring People handle personal information."
>
  <article class="privacy-policy">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Effective September 7, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This policy explains how Leon Lin operates leonlins.com and the Avoid
      Boring People newsletter. Questions can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:contact@leonlins.com">contact@leonlins.com</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Information collected</h2>
    <p>
      If you subscribe to the newsletter, the information involved is your
      email address, subscription and consent records, confirmation and
      unsubscribe records, and limited security information used to prevent
      abusive sign-up attempts. The website may also receive standard technical
      information from your browser and hosting providers, such as IP address,
      device/browser details, and pages requested.
    </p>

    <h2>How information is used</h2>
    <p>
      Information is used to operate the site and newsletter, confirm a
      subscription, deliver requested writing, honour unsubscribe requests,
      prevent abuse, and maintain the security and reliability of the service.
      Newsletter data is not sold.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter providers and legacy subscriptions</h2>
    <p>
      The current public newsletter sign-up form is operated by Substack. If
      you subscribe through it, Substack also processes your information under
      its own terms and privacy practices. The planned owned newsletter uses
      Neon for subscriber records and Amazon Web Services Simple Email Service
      (SES) for delivery and delivery-event processing. The site is hosted on
      Vercel. These providers process information only as needed to provide
      their services.
    </p>
    <p>
      If legacy Substack subscribers are migrated in the future, the retained
      information will be limited to the subscription, consent, and suppression
      history needed to provide the newsletter and prevent accidental
      resubscription of people who opted out.
    </p>

    <h2>Choices and retention</h2>
    <p>
      Every newsletter will include an unsubscribe link. You can also contact
      <a href="mailto:contact@leonlins.com">contact@leonlins.com</a> for
      help with your subscription or privacy questions. Suppression records may
      be retained after an unsubscribe request as needed to honour that request
      and avoid sending you future newsletter email by mistake.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and third-party content</h2>
    <p>
      The site may use privacy-conscious Google Analytics configuration when
      enabled and embeds third-party services such as Giscus for article
      comments. Those services may collect information under their own privacy
      policies. This site does not currently use newsletter engagement tracking
      or behavioural advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, privacy law may give you rights to request
      access, correction, deletion, restriction, or objection to certain uses
      of personal information. Contact
      <a href="mailto:contact@leonlins.com">contact@leonlins.com</a> to make
      a request. You may also have the right to complain to the privacy
      regulator where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated when the site or newsletter changes. The
      effective date above will be updated when material changes are published.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-policy {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .updated {
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    margin-top: -1rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
